   "displayId": "textTurn_exploreDataFromNL_1794701200000_closing",
   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**Nearly every pupil reaches minimum reading proficiency by the end of primary school in Canada, Russia and Hong Kong.** The highest shares:\n\n- **Canada:** 98.8% (2021)\n- **Russia:** 98.4% (2021)\n- **Hong Kong:** 98.3% (2021)\n- **Croatia:** 98.1% (2021)\n- **Italy:** 97.2% (2021)\n\nAt the other end, fewer than half of pupils reach it in 48 of the 101 countries with a recent assessment. The dashboard shows how countries spread between the two, with the highest and lowest; the map beside it shows where they are. Each country's latest assessment from 2018–2025. Source: UIS, November 2026 release; indicator READ.PRIMARY.",
